id: pm-6qiwan
title: "Provide consistent tracker preflight and executable recovery across SDK, CLI, and MCP"
description: "Promote tracker-initialization detection into one public SDK guard and migrate the 48 hand-rolled CLI call sites to it. The shared primitive must distinguish missing roots, file collisions, and missing settings with precise recovery and a static replication gate."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: "area:sdk",defect-recurrence,error-taxonomy,refactor,simplification
created_at: "2026-08-10T05:54:06.969Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-20T09:43:07.641Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-20T09:19:13.983Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-20T09:19:13.983Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "A single SDK guard owns the tracker-initialization refusal and all 48 call sites delegate to it; The guard distinguishes root-missing, root-is-a-file, and settings-missing, and each carries its own recovery; The recovery for root-is-a-file does not suggest pm init, which cannot succeed against a regular file; The surface-replication gate declares this set so a 49th hand-rolled copy fails CI"
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Centralized tracker initialization and readability behind public SDK primitives, migrated all CLI and MCP entrypoints, added typed executable recovery and fail-closed source ratchets, and closed every hosted review portability and cleanup gap."
expected_result: "Every SDK, CLI, and MCP tracker consumer uses one precise preflight contract; malformed ratchet declarations fail closed; recovery and test fixtures remain executable, portable, and race-safe."
actual_result: "All 50 preflight sites across 45 SDK modules delegate to the shared guard; four filesystem states have typed recovery; explicit null ratchets are rejected; unique OS temp fixtures, 22 probes, packed npm/npx/bunx acceptance, and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage pass."
component: "sdk/* command entrypoints, core/store/item-store"
